<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

	<!--
		A join that needs Heaven and Hell OR Vampires and the Undead rather than Heaven and Hell alone.
		  - Nephilim Xenotype Reborn's halo gene gains Big and Small's BS_Halo exclusion tag, so a pawn cannot wear
		    both mods' halos at once. Verified: the Heaven and Hell halo gene does carry that tag.

		Gating, which is why this is its own folder: the demon xenotypes (the original reason for the folder) are not Heaven and Hell or Vampires and the
		Undead defs. Big and Small - Genes &amp; More defines them, inside a folder its own LoadFolders only loads when
		RedMattis.Undead or RedMattis.Heaven is active. This folder mirrors that exact condition, which is also what
		the original any-of mod check came to.
		The mod gates sit on <li> nodes inside sequences, not on the <Operation> itself: RimWorld reads
		MayRequire only on list elements, so an <Operation MayRequire="..."> node loads and applies
		unconditionally.
		Name fix applied on review: the original checked for a mod named "Nephilim Xenotype". Mod-name checks
		are exact matches and the mod is named "Nephilim Xenotype Reborn", so those checks never fired. The
		packageId sov.nephilim is used here instead, which cannot drift the same way.
		The original sat behind a Too Many Mods setting toggle (TMM_BS_NephilimBeliarIntegration, default on).
		That toggle is dropped: the folder gate and the MayRequire checks already keep it inert unless the
		mods it joins are installed.

		Verified against the current 1.6 releases: the Nephilim halo base already has an exclusionTags list so the add
		lands.
		The demon xenotypes' Beliar racism gene was removed on 2026-09-29 (the user dropped all Beliar racism content).
	-->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationSequence">
		<operations>
			<li Class="PatchOperationSequence" MayRequire="sov.nephilim">
				<operations>
					<li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
						<xpath>
							Defs/GeneDef[@Name="GS_HaloBaseNEW"]/exclusionTags</xpath>
						<value>
							<li>BS_Halo</li>
						</value>
					</li>
				</operations>
			</li>
		</operations>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
